From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DER/32-Project <der32@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 16:41:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] amd64: add DER32 kernel configuration

Derived from GENERIC by inclusion; keeps every GENERIC driver so the kernel
boots on QEMU/KVM and real hardware.  DER/32-specific deltas go here.
---
 sys/arch/amd64/conf/DER32 | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 sys/arch/amd64/conf/DER32

diff --git a/sys/arch/amd64/conf/DER32 b/sys/arch/amd64/conf/DER32
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3c5fdde7259d3c0a4aaebde06a4093799a189237
--- /dev/null
+++ b/sys/arch/amd64/conf/DER32
@@ -0,0 +1,13 @@
+#	$DER32: DER32,v 0.1 2026/11/19 $
+#
+# DER32 -- DER/32 kernel configuration for amd64.
+#
+# Derived from NetBSD GENERIC.  Milestone 0/1 keeps every GENERIC driver so
+# that the kernel boots on QEMU/KVM (IDE/AHCI/virtio disks, e1000/virtio
+# network, ns16550 serial console) as well as real hardware.  DER/32-specific
+# divergence from GENERIC is expressed below as explicit additions/removals so
+# the delta stays reviewable.
+
+include 	"arch/amd64/conf/GENERIC"
+
+ident		"DER32"
